   :review "Records read myself with edn/read in a loop. VERIFIED: 20 records; :controller-score in 20/20; :prediction-mean in 20/20; :f-pi-by-candidate-id in 20/20, one :absent envelope at tick 1 (cold start, correct) and 19 :present. THE RANK-PROXY LIMIT IS LIFTED. Every rank measurement in this campaign -- the 82-of-110 reshuffle, the argmax claims, the V6 arms -- was over a G-total proxy, because the July fields carried :G-total but not the score rank-actions sorted on. These records carry it. Those measurements are RE-RUNNABLE AT THE MACHINE OWN GRAIN and should be re-run before any of them is quoted again. ONE DEFECT THAT BLOCKS R3: :wm/route IS ABSENT FROM ALL 20 TRACE FORMS. The tick computes the route -- the receipt carries :route and :route-verdict -- but trace-record does not persist it, and the receipt is one file per DATE overwritten each tick, so nineteen routes were lost and only tick 20 survives. Conformance cannot be checked against a run whose routes were not kept. Opened RUN10. AND THE FINDING, from the one route we have. Tick 20: R20->R12, R12->R2, R2->R7, R7->R3, R3->R8, R8->R5, R5->R6, R6->R14, R14->TRACE. Checked against control-map-edges.edn -- against the registry :decisions :retires set, NOT the list in the campaign brief, which I nearly used and which does NOT match the registry. TWO HOPS TRAVERSE RETIRED EDGES: R2->R7, retired by :r2-r7-superseded-by-eps on the grounds that R7 imports the prediction errors and not the observation; and R5->R6. CORRECTED SAME DAY after claude-1 pushed on the grain question: my first pass checked :edges ONLY and missed :route-measured-drawn, so I reported five hops as unmapped. NONE ARE. All nine are accounted for -- five route-measured (R20->R12, R12->R2, R3->R8, R6->R14, R14->TRACE), two drawn (R7->R3, R8->R5), two retired and discussed below. ALSO ESTABLISHED so nobody re-derives it: seven of the eight retired pairs are still :status :drawn in :edges, and that is BY DESIGN -- gen_live_topology.bb:133 says