  {:id :RUN7 :class :RUN :status :done :reviewed-by "codex" :reviewed-at "2026-09-01T19:56:51Z" :covers-key :none :review "Read all four evidence diffs (039b0b8, ed2be78, b5da2bf, cf36ac1) and confirmed none touches aif-equations.edn or control-map-edges.edn. Re-ran 116 tests / 492 assertions across war-machine, trace, policy-precision, run-tick-once and wm-run-lock: 0 failures, 0 errors; clj-kondo 0 errors / 0 warnings; check-parens exit 0. The real pre-flight exited 0 after 25.6 s with 0 POSTs, 0 .admintoken reads and the run lock released. Independent arms script exited 0: 20/20 usable fields, solver-control delta 0.0, and all 20 recorded betas reproduced at delta 0.00e+00; beta_0=1.0 carried beta 1.002646073 -> 1.034342317, gamma 0.997360910 -> 0.966797920, with 20/20 converged and bracketed. Grep found policy-precision-state readers only at beta-dark-carry, trace persistence, and the arms reader; the pinned 183749a trace predates the field. pointer_check: 246 pointers / 0 unresolved; negative_controls: PASS (16 negative, 10 positive). The converged-and-bracketed carry rule is coherent with the subsequently recorded b2 fallback: unsolved ticks hold the carried variational beta and do not cross to the selection-gain law." :owner-did "2026-09-01, claude-20 (CLI work seat)" :unblocked-by "wm-build-loop: depends-on all :done" :depends-on [:RUN3 :RUN12 :RUN11]
   :evidence "futon2 039b0b8 (the carry) + ed2be78 (pre-flight repair) + b5da2bf (arms script) + cf36ac1 (the run, the arms, C468). Run dir holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/2026-09-01-s2/ with README.md, ARMS.txt, CONFORMANCE.txt, wm-trace-s2.edn and 20 receipts. THE CARRY: src/futon2/aif/policy_precision.clj (initial-beta-state / coerce-state / beta-for / held-state / align-f-pi-and-g / carry-beta), read-coerce-fold-write shaped on selection-gain deliberately so this apparatus has one cross-tick state pattern; FUTON_WM_BETA_DARK and beta-dark-carry at scripts/futon2/report/war_machine.clj:236-283; :policy-precision-state persisted present-only at src/futon2/aif/trace.clj:572-581. ONLY A SOLVED POSTERIOR CARRIES -- converged? AND bracketed? -- and an unsolved or fieldless tick HOLDS its prior as :held-unsolved / :held-absent with no stale :solve riding forward, so a reader can tell solved from held (the constraint I1(b) put on this slice). FLAG-OFF BYTE-IDENTITY proven cross-version against a PINNED sha 183749a, not HEAD~, and the existing F_pi control repinned to it -- the RUN5 review finding that a moving anchor turns the claim into 'the last commit changed nothing'. NOTHING CONSUMES IT: grep over src, scripts and holes shows the only readers of :policy-precision-state are beta-dark-carry (its own carry) and the trace writer. GATES: clj-kondo 0/0; check-parens OK; 109 tests / 448 assertions across war-machine, trace, policy-precision, run-tick-once and wm-run-lock, 0 failures 0 errors; p4ng negative_controls PASS (16 negative, 10 positive); pointer_check 215/0. THE RUN: 20/20 ticks exit 0, 78-93 s each (mean 84), 18:39:18-19:07 UTC, one run lock, pre-flight PASS on the same tree immediately before (0 POSTs, 0 .admintoken reads). 20/20 records :status :present :beta-source :converged-posterior, converged and bracketed, 145 aligned candidates (143 cold start). beta 1.000 -> 1.034342317 monotone, gamma 0.99736 -> 0.96680. Cost 646 bytes on a 1,045,650-byte record, 0.0618%