   :review "Read all of futon2 5a24194 and checked the binding reorder: the moved ranking/cascade/F_pi/beta bindings use inputs already available at their new position and feed the same wm-ranked+cascades field into selection. Re-ran the nine named namespaces: 202 tests, 865 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors (exit 0). Re-ran both real-environment preflights: control tau 1.0 from :selection-gain-only with no beta, S3 tau 1.0364658677086602 exactly equal to the tick beta, :tau-source :converged-posterior, gamma 0.9648171070126254, 0 POSTs, 0 .admintoken reads, and lock released; both exit 0. Re-ran run8_tau_arms.clj (exit 0): all 60 control ticks reproduced score/order/softmax at delta 0.0; across S1, S1b and S2, 0 controller-rank, habit-rank, habit-argmax, or softmax-argmax moves, smallest cross-group margin +0.7355590795, and mean softmax TV 0.0003573076 / 0.0003572421 / 0.0003571305. The monotonicity claim is correct within equal-ln-E groups because -G/tau preserves G order for positive tau; the measured positive cross-group margin covers the remaining adjacent comparisons. Confirmed neither registry changed. pointer_check: 264 pointers in 3 files, 0 unresolved (exit 0); worklist_check exit 0."
