   :evidence "futon2 5a24194. THE PAIR, changed together as the acceptance requires because one throws on a mode the other admits: the parser is tau-mode-of at war_machine.clj:494-508 -- extracted as a PURE fn so a test drives it with strings instead of mutating the environment -- with arena-tau-mode at war_machine.clj:510-528 being that fn applied to the env read and nothing else; the closed dispatch is policy.clj:76-145, tau_eff = beta exactly, with g and tau_spread BOTH out of the expression. NEVER CROSSES LAWS (I1 b2b (2)): carry-beta always yields a finite positive beta (policy_precision.clj:544-560), so a tick that did not both converge and bracket HOLDS upstream and the new :tau-source names which law produced each tick's tau -- policy.clj:56-75 temperature-source, emitted at policy.clj:318,369,519,547 and persisted (strip-decision drops only :softmax-weights and :ranked-actions, trace.clj:168-178). No beta at all THROWS rather than reverting to 1/g (policy.clj:134-142), and the test asserts the throw is not mistakable for the 1/g answer. variational-tau-preconditions! (war_machine.clj:102-130) refuses the mode without FUTON_WM_BETA_DARK / FUTON_WM_FPI_DARK / FUTON_WM_TRACE_POLICY_DETAILS, where every tick would hold beta_0 at tau = 1.0 -- correct, useless, and indistinguishable in a record from a converged carry sitting at 1.0. STRUCTURAL CHANGE, stated because it is the risk: the beta solve is the temperature, so it must precede selection; cascade-policies/cascade-actions/wm-ranked+cascades (war_machine.clj:4903-4931) and the two dark-field bindings (war_machine.clj:4932-4948) moved ahead of controller-decision. Pure let bindings, all inputs bound earlier, nothing between reads them, same join field wm-ranked+cascades so the beta series stays comparable with S2. THE LIVE PATH RAN, TWICE (run8_s3_preflight.clj, env set in the shell so the parser reads the real environment): control tau 1.0 / :tau-source :selection-gain-only / no beta computed; S3 tau 1.0364669814843985 = the solved beta EXACTLY, :tau-source :converged-posterior, gamma 0.9648160702310347, :wm-version :tau-mode :variational-beta-gamma, continuing the S2 carry which closed at 1.034342317. 0 POSTs and 0 .admintoken reads on both, run lock taken and released. Default-path r6_zero_post_preflight PASS in 29.7 s after the reorder. THE MOVEMENT (run8_tau_arms.clj, runs/2026-09-01-s3/ARMS.txt), 3 fields x 20 ticks x 145 candidates, replayed with policy/softmax-weights and policy/effective-temperature THEMSELVES rather than a re-implementation. CONTROL FIRST: at tau_live the replay reproduces each record's own -G/tau scores, :habit-adjusted-ranking order and :softmax-weights-by-candidate-id at delta 0.0 on 60/60 ticks. Only S2 solved a beta series (20 ticks, 1.0026460727 -> 1.0343423166, all :converged-posterior); S1 and S1b persisted no F_pi readback so their beta is NOT recoverable and the arm transplants S2's by tick index -- stated, not hidden, which makes the S1 arm 'the S1 field under the temperatures S2 measured'. RESULT, all three fields: 0 controller rank moves, 0 habit-adjusted rank moves, 0 habit argmax moves, 0 softmax argmax moves; mean softmax TV distance 3.57e-4, mean entropy 4.66727 -> 4.66725 (S1). AND THE ZEROS ARE STRUCTURAL RATHER THAN A NEAR MISS: ordering is by ln E - G/tau, so raising tau adds +G(1/tau_live - 1/tau_s3) to every score, MONOTONE in G, so within one ln E value the order cannot change at all; ln E takes 3 distinct values (spread 3.0445 nats) and the smallest cross-group adjacent margin at tau_s3 is +0.7356, where negative would be a flip. STALE LABELS corrected in the same slice as the row asks: dark_mode_shadow.bb:9-20,128-140,160,170 called the live mode :gamma-only and bound (:decision :selection-gain) to a variable named gamma; the mode has been :selection-gain-only since B-2d and g is the R14 ENGINEERING gain, whose name collides with the variational gamma = 1/beta this row puts on the live path. No computation changed, on