   :reviewer-should-check "(1) WHERE THE HASH IS TAKEN. I moved the file read inside mission_c/read-criteria from slurp to readAllBytes-then-decode so one read serves both the digest and the parse. That is a change to the READER, not just to the record, and it is the substantive judgement in this row. If you think the digest belongs at the war_machine seam (hash the path next to :criteria-source, leaving read-criteria alone), say so -- it is a smaller diff and it reintroduces a TOCTOU window between the hash and the read, which is the thing U12 asked to close. (2) THE ENCODING CLAIM at mission_c.clj:281-283. I assert (String. bytes \"UTF-8\") reproduces what slurp decoded, on the basis that clojure.java.io's default encoding is the literal \"UTF-8\" and not the platform charset. If that is wrong, a non-UTF-8 criteria file now parses differently than before, which would be a silent behaviour change in a row that claims none. Verify it rather than take it. (3) THE TWO PINNED CONSTANTS in war_machine_test.clj:1633's u12-recorded-source-sha256. They are content hashes of two files that are live in this repo -- holes/missions/M-wm-aif-policy-grain-compliance.md is an ordinary mission doc anyone may edit -- so this test WILL break the day someone edits it, by design. Decide whether that tripwire is wanted in the suite or belongs in a replay script under runs/; if the former, check the docstring says clearly enough that the repair is re-measure-and-update-both, not update-the-pin. (4) PRESENT-ONLY VS ALWAYS-PRESENT. The acceptance says the readback map CARRIES :criteria-source-sha256; I made it present-only, so a readback with :criteria-reason :source-not-found has :criteria-source (a path) and no digest. A reviewer who reads the acceptance as always-present should say so -- the alternative is an explicit typed value (:no-bytes-read) rather than nil, and I did not want to invent a second vocabulary for something :criteria-reason already says. (5) THAT NOTHING LEAKED: git s