   :bar {:a "Not decidable from sources, code or a prior ruling. The theory says C is a normalised preference density over outcomes; it does not say what an OUTCOME IS when the spec is Bernoulli and the observable is a continuous [0,1] health channel. No equation in aif-equations.edn imports an outcome type; the criteria are prose written by people (holes/missions/*.md IDENTIFY sections) and none of the nine in the corpus declares a :spec, a threshold or an observable kind. The registry already records this as Joe's: :c-grain :flip-is-j-gated calls the repair beneath preferences.clj:242-244 'a decision about what an OUTCOME IS for a Bernoulli criterion (==, a threshold, or a refusal to score a continuous observable against a Bernoulli C at all), not a typo to patch' -- which is the three arms, named before they were built."
