         :why-not-runnable "The branches ARE built and ARE run -- futon2 dae82dc, artifact runs/U16-outcome-semantics/ -- so this row does not ask Joe for an advance ruling. It asks him after the numbers, which is what his rule of 2026-09-01 asks for. What is not runnable is the discriminating experiment: the arms differ on values whose intended reading exists only in the prose the criteria are written in, so no tick, replay or sweep can prefer one. STATED AGAINST MYSELF: if the bar is read as 'arms that cannot be run', this row fails it, since these ran. It is minted under the reading that the bar is about the DISCRIMINATING experiment, not about the arms' buildability, and U16 :reviewer-should-check (5) records that as the weakest part of the row."}
   :statement "WHAT IS A BERNOULLI OUTCOME when the observable is continuous? U12 found log-preference's Bernoulli branch selects the non-target pole with (= 0 x), false for the double 0.0, so R2's observation vector cannot reach the unsatisfied pole and nil reads as met (preferences.clj:242). U16 built and ran the three candidate readings; all three fix the defect and none is preferred by any number. THE ARMS AND WHAT EACH COSTS, measured over the 14-channel sweep and the U12 corpus: (1) :numeric-equality -- == rather than =, needs no declaration, scores every channel (14/14, 2 distinct risk values), and calls 0.75 a MET criterion, so a channel two thirds of the way to its target is scored as satisfied. (2) :declared-binarization -- a Bernoulli spec on a continuous observable must carry a threshold; scores 4/14 (the channels reading exactly 0), refuses the rest :no-declared-threshold, and with a threshold declared scores 14/14 and reads 0.75 as unmet or met depending on where the threshold is put. (3) :typed-binary-only -- refuse on spec/observable mismatch, == for genuinely binary observables; scores 0/14 because no criterion declares an observable kind, and 4/14 once one does. Under all three, nil is a typed absence rather than a satisfied criterion, which is C130 discipline and not one of the branches. Arms 2 and 3 are indistinguishable at the composition on this corpus and part company only where a declaration exists. THE QUESTION: should a criterion whose observable carries no declaration be SCORED on the type fix alone, or REFUSED until someone writes the declaration down? Scoring gives the mission-grain C numbers on every tick at the price of calling most readings satisfied; refusing gives it a typed absence on nearly every tick until the mission documents are amended, which is work on nine criteria across two missions and everything written later. NOT PART OF THIS QUESTION, because U16 measured them settled: clause (b) is unchanged by every arm (risk_mis is