   :supersedes :U13
   :superseded-by :U18
   :reviewed-by "codex" :reviewed-at "2026-09-02T19:46:59Z"
   :review-covers "7ad831a525bf732bf163a9a6ab69e29fefb08fbb"
   :review "Reviewed futon2 f257ff8 and ledger commit 1f4f0c3 (Joseph Corneli). The excess form for :range removes exactly log Z, leaving gap/T: zero throughout the declared band, positive immediately outside it, and non-negative across the tested range shapes and temperatures; leaving :bernoulli unshifted is correct because its point-mass term is already the exact discrete KL, not the continuous cross-entropy whose arbitrary constant U17 repairs. The finite non-negative weight guard is necessary for the composition-level claim, and the record preserves the prior cross-entropy plus the named shift while contributions sum to :risk. At the evidence/ledger commit, preferences-cdist-test passed 19 tests/785 assertions, mission-c-test 25/2622, and war-machine-test 66/351, all with 0 failures/errors. At current HEAD those last two namespaces have one unrelated fixture-shape failure each after the later 161ac09 mission-document change; the U17 evidence checkout is green. clj-kondo 0 errors/warnings; check-parens OK; pointer_check 912 pointers/0 unresolved; negative_controls PASS (18 negative, 11 positive). Signed the current additive :choices :c-grain entry; no source, registry, generator, or figure changed in this review."
   :statement "Range-spec composition hazard from U12 clause (c): inside the declared band the range branch's term is ln Z, NEGATIVE (-0.512 for [0.5 1.0] at 0.75), so summing risk_mis with C_int's KL (>= 0) in one G would pay a satisfied range criterion a BONUS. The codebase already solved this class once: kl-gaussian-range (preferences.clj, directly below the defect) exists because 'the untruncated form was a divergence score that could dip below 0'. Fix direction: route range criteria through a proper KL >= 0 (or clamp with the choice recorded), consistent with whatever U16 rules an outcome is."
   :acceptance "risk_mis provably >= 0 on every spec shape (property test over range/bernoulli specs including in-band values); the chosen form recorded in the :c-grain registry entry; no satisfied criterion scores below an unsatisfied one on the same channel."
   :evidence "futon2 f257ff8 (code, tests, registry) and this commit (ledger). WHAT WAS WRONG, AND IT IS ONLY THE RANGE BRANCH. Under the v0 point-mass forward model the per-criterion term was the surprisal -ln C_k(o_k). For a :bernoulli C that IS the KL exactly -- KL(delta_b || C) = -ln C(b) >= 0 because C(b) <= 1, already pinned against pref/kl by mission_c_test/surprisal-is-the-point-mass-kl -- so the Bernoulli branch was never the hazard. For a :range C it is NOT a KL: a point mass has no density on a continuous support, KL(delta_x || C) is +infinity at every x, and what the code carried is the CROSS-ENTROPY gap/T + ln Z, fixed only up to an additive constant. Z < 1 for any band narrower than one unit, so ln Z < 0 and a criterion read INSIDE its own declared band scored NEGATIVE. Pinned to the digit as U17 wrote it: -0.5119492459595545 for [0.5 1.0] at T = 0.1 (preferences_cdist_test/the-unshifted-range-term-is-the-negative-U17-names, preferences_cdist_test.clj:216). THE FORM CHOSEN, of the two the row named: the EXCESS, KL(delta_x || C) - inf_y KL(delta_y || C) = gap/T, where the divergent point-mass entropy cancels between the two terms and ln Z with it (preferences.clj:375-439 -- the reasoning block at :375, point-mass-divergence-shift at :415, point-mass-divergence at :429). NOT THE CLAMP (max 0.0 (+ (/ gap T) log-z)): it also clears zero, but it flattens the gradient for a further -T ln Z outside the band -- 0.0512 for [0.5 1.0] at T = 0.1 -- so a value missing the band by 0.05 would read as fully satisfied, where the excess form scores it 0.5 (mission_c_test/a-satisfied-range-criterion-no-longer-scores-below-zero, mission_c_test.clj:427). Same repair class as kl-gaussian-range (preferences.clj:441), which the row cites and which exists because 'the untruncated form was a divergence score that could dip below 0'. THE BERNOULLI BRANCH IS DELIBERATELY NOT SHIFTED, which is the second half of the choice and the reason no committed number moves: its shift is 0.0, so subtracting its own minimum -ln max(p1, 1-p1) -- the 4.539889921682063E-5 T=0.1 satisfied floor U12 and U16 measured -- was NOT done. That floor is a real property of a soft target, not the missing-constant artefact the range branch has, and removing it would move numbers the two committed replay artifacts pin. U12 clause (c)'s satisfied-zero therefore stays unreached for Bernoulli criteria, exactly as U16 recorded it. NO NUMBER IN THE CORPUS MOVES AT ALL: default-spec is {:becomes 1} (mission_c.clj:67-74) and no criterion in the U12/U16 corpus declares a :spec (U16), so divergence-shift (mission_c.clj:419) is 0.0 over the whole corpus and the range branch is so far reached only from tests -- runs/U12-c-mis-falsifier/ and runs/U16-outcome-semantics/ were NOT re-run and NOT edited. THE PRE-U17 NUMBER IS KEPT, NOT OVERWRITTEN: risk-mis records :cross-entropy (the unshifted sum) and :divergence-shift beside :risk, and per criterion :surprisal beside :divergence and :shift; :contribution is w_k times the divergence, so the recorded contributions still sum to :risk and war_machine_test.clj:1719-1720's identity holds unchanged (mission_c.clj:436-501). ORTHOGONAL TO J6, so this row did not wait on it: the shift is a function of the SPEC KIND alone and never of which outcome an arm reads, identical under every U16 arm and under none (mission_c_test/the-shift-is-the-same-under-every-arm, mission_c_test.clj:486). THE PROPERTY TEST the acceptance asks for: mission_c_test/risk-mis-is-nonnegative-on-every-spec-shape (mission_c_test.clj:407) sweeps 9 specs (5 range including the degenerate [0.2 0.2] and the whole-support [0.0 1.0], 4 Bernoulli) x 3 temperatures x 9 values INCLUDING in-band ones x 4 readings of an outcome (no arm plus each U16 arm) and asserts risk >= 0, every per-criterion divergence >= 0, and contributions summing to risk; preferences_cdist_test/point-mass-divergence-is-nonnegative-on-every-spec-shape (preferences_cdist_test.clj:230) does the density level