   :reviewer-should-check "(1) THE ASYMMETRY IS THE JUDGEMENT IN THIS ROW. I shifted :range and left :bernoulli alone, on the argument that the Bernoulli term is an exact KL with no missing constant while the range term is a cross-entropy whose constant was never fixed. The uniform alternative -- subtract each kind's own minimum, so a fully satisfied criterion of ANY shape scores exactly 0 -- is arguably more coherent as a composition and would make U12 clause (c)'s satisfied-zero reachable at last. I did not take it because it moves the 4.539889921682063E-5 that runs/U12-c-mis-falsifier/measurements.edn and runs/U16-outcome-semantics/measurements.edn both record, and because that floor is a genuine property of a soft Bernoulli target rather than an artefact. If you read the acceptance's 'provably >= 0 on every spec shape' as asking for the uniform form, say so -- it is a small change to point-mass-divergence-shift and a large change to what the two artifacts mean. (2) THE THIRD LIMB'S WORDING. 'No satisfied criterion scores below an unsatisfied one on the same channel' is ambiguous in sign, because risk_mis is a cost and 'below' could be lower-cost (which is what you WANT of a satisfied criterion) or worse-merit. I tested both readings rather than pick one; check that the ordering test is the one you meant, and that testing both is not hiding a third reading. (3) LOSING ln Z FROM THE RANGE TERM IS A REAL CONSEQUENCE, not just a constant. Before the shift a NARROW band carried a large negative ln Z, so a narrow criterion was cheaper everywhere than a wide one at the same gap; after it, band width enters only through the gap. That is a change in how two range criteria compare to each other, not only in whether one dips below zero, and no test pins the old cross-criterion ordering because nothing consumed it. (4) I CHANGED risk-mis's :risk RATHER THAN ADDING AN ARM, unlike U16. The argument is that U17 asks for a fix ('route range criteria through a proper KL >= 0'), not a comparison, and that risk_mis is read by nothing on a default tick -- FUTON_WM_MISSION_C is off and mission-c-fields binds after selection is final. If you think this needed the U16 treatment (a selector, default unchanged), that is a structural objection to the whole commit and worth making now. (5) THE WEIGHT GUARD IS SCOPE I ADDED. c-mis now throws on a declared weight that is negative, NaN or infinite. It was not in the acceptance; I added it because 'provably >= 0' is false without it. It can reject a caller that previously worked, though no caller in the tree declares weights at all (grep for :criterion-weights: mission_c.clj and mission_c_test.clj only). (6) THAT NOTHING LEAKED: git show --stat f257ff8 touches six files -- two src, three test, aif-equations.edn -- no p4ng file, no generator, nothing under data/ or runs/. holes/labs/wm-contract/workflow-report.edn and the three untracked tick-run-record-2026-09-02-*.edn files were already in the working tree when I arrived and are NOT mine; I staged explicit paths, not -a."}
