   :reviewer-should-check "(1) THE DEFAULT MOVED, WHICH IS THE BIGGEST THING HERE. risk-mis with :outcome-semantics omitted no longer returns the raw pref/log-preference number; it returns the ruled arm's, which on the U12 corpus is a typed ABSENCE where a number used to be. That is what J6 chose, but it means every future replay of U12's script differs from its committed artifact in the two places named in :evidence, and I did NOT re-run either artifact. Decide whether U12's runs/ directory should be re-measured under the ruling as its own row, or left as the record of what the machine did before it. (2) THE EXPLICIT-NIL ESCAPE. I kept the pre-ruling path reachable by passing :outcome-semantics nil explicitly, relying on Clojure's :or defaulting only on an ABSENT key. It is exactly the semantics I want and it is pinned by a test, but it is a subtle distinction to leave load on: a caller who writes :outcome-semantics (get opts :arm) and gets nil silently takes the defective path. The alternative is a named fourth value (:pre-J6-raw) and no reliance on nil, which is louder and adds a vocabulary member. Say if you want that. (3) THE MIRROR CONTROL IN U16'S SCRIPT NOW PRINTS 'CONTROL: FAILS -- do not read section 4'. It fails correctly -- it compares the script's mirror against the shipped readback and the shipped readback took the ruling -- but a future re-runner sees a red control on a green change. I left the script untouched because editing an artifact producer would stale the artifact it produced; the other repair is to teach the mirror the ruled arm and regenerate, which rewrites a measurement record. Neither is obviously right and it is not my call. (4) THE GAUGE TABLE LISTS SIX KEYS FOR THREE CRITERIA, one per id vocabulary, on the claim that futon2 161ac09 ported the ingest's three criteria into the doc verbatim and in order. I verified the order by reading both files; nothing enforces it, so if someone reorders the doc's numbered list the doc ids silently bin