   :reviewer-should-check "(1) THE NUMBER. The acceptance names 3.333378732232873 and the replay reports 6.666712065566529. Check that the difference is the third observable and nothing else: runs/U42-producers/U42-PRODUCERS.txt section 2 is the per-observable agreement table against U21's committed probe (two agree, :registry-gap-list-present does not). (2) THE JUDGEMENT that :registry-gap-list-present is 0.0 rather than a typed absence. The reading taken: the observable is 'is the gap list WHERE THE REGISTRY POINTS', so a registry that points nowhere ANSWERS it, and the absence path is reserved for a registry that will not read (mission_gauges.clj:217-243, both arms tested at mission_gauges_test.clj:102 and :114). The other reading -- 'the producer cannot read its artifact, so type it' -- would leave the criterion unmeasurable and 4abad68c at 2/3, which is a different acceptance. If the reviewer prefers that reading, the change is one branch. (3) THE GATE RECEIPT is a live read pinned in bytes, so confirm it is honest: runs/U42-producers/gate-receipt.edn records the store endpoint, the report_gate.clj and z1_views.clj sha256s, and the exact decision adjudicated. Re-run `bb holes/labs/wm-contract/u42_gate_receipt.bb` -- it re-picks the newest recorded zaif decision by text search, so a different subject with the same verdict is expected drift and a different VERDICT is a finding. (4) NON-CONSUMPTION. war_machine.clj:5954-5977: the merge target is the readback's argument, not the `observation` binding. Grep that no other caller of mission-c-readback was changed and that the *mission-c?* gate still wraps the whole thing. (5) A CANDIDATE ROW, NOT MINTED HERE (the loop takes one item and this row's acceptance did not ask for it): aif-equations.edn declares no gap-list pointer, so :honest-gap-list-published cannot be satisfied by any amount of work on the gap list itself. The repair is a registry write pointing at holes/labs/zaif-harness/runs/U10-node-coverage.edn (or C489-u6-zaif-full-loop.md section 6), which is Joe's to make. Until it lands, M-zaif-harness-v1 carries one criterion that is unsatisfiable by construction. (6) THE AMENDMENT IS THE WHOLE OF THIS SECOND PASS and it relaxes a bar, so read it against the two things that would make it self-serving. Check that the probe's 1.0 really was STIPULATED and not measured -- u21_selection_focus.clj:70-79 declares the three values by hand under a comment that says so; if U21 measured that 1.0 anywhere, the amendment is wrong and the producer is. Check that aif-equations.edn points NOWHERE rather than pointing somewhere the producer does not look: it reads :zaif-node-gap-list on the registry root and :gap-list on any :equations entry and nothing else (mission_gauges.clj:198-216), so a pointer under a third name would be a defect in the producer rather than a measurement. The registry's top-level keys are :as-of :choices :equations :exogenous :holes :owner :plumbing :plumbing-notes :references :schema :sources :verified. (7) NOTHING ELSE MOVED IN THE SECOND PASS: it touches worklist.edn only -- no src/, no test/, no p4ng file, nothing under runs/ or data/. The replay was re-run to /tmp/U42-verify precisely so runs/U42-producers/ stays byte-identical to 9973bba, and it reproduced all three producer values, the 2/3 agreement table and 6.666712065566529 at exit 0. (8) THE THIRD PASS REPAIRS A GATE, so read it against the two ways that goes wrong. FIRST, did it fix the gate or move the goalposts? The check's subject is schema compatibility and :failures was already [] at the red run -- the red came from :reader-census, from a date written into the source at f7fba13 and never bumped. Check the arithmetic: 79 records in wm-trace-2026-09-01.edn plus 3 in -09-02.edn against 885 - 803. If you read the fixed window as a deliberate corpus pin rather than a stale constant, the change is wrong and the repair is a bump instead; nothing in f7fba13 or the file's comments says pin, and data/ is unt