   :acceptance-amended "2026-09-03, second pass, answering the reopen; the acceptance below is kept verbatim and ONE CLAUSE OF IT IS REPLACED HERE. THE CLAUSE: the replay must report \"risk_mis 3.333378732232873 on 4abad68c's observation\" with the probe removed from the path. That number is not a measurement and no producer reading an artifact can return it. It is what the readback yields when :registry-gap-list-present is 1.0, and that 1.0 was STIPULATED: u21_selection_focus.clj:70-79 declares the three probe values by hand under a comment naming them as declared, and U21's own evidence states the number CONDITIONALLY -- supply exactly those three observables and it returns 3.333378732232873. The acceptance dropped the condition and kept the number. U18 had already flagged the same inheritance about the 3/3 it passed on (its :reviewer-should-check point 5: \"the 3/3 in the acceptance is with the values supplied by a test\"). WHAT THE ARTIFACT SAYS INSTEAD, checked this pass rather than carried from the first: the criterion is :honest-gap-list-published, \"which R nodes zaif exercises vs stubs, recorded where the registry points\", carrier \"aif-equations.edn + U6 artifact\" (S4-identify-ingest.edn:32); aif-equations.edn carries no gap-list pointer under any name -- five strings contain \"gap\" and none is a pointer, three contain \"zaif\" and none names a coverage artifact, and the top-level key set holds nothing of the kind. So 0.0 is what the criterion's own carrier returns, and reproducing 3.333378732232873 would mean emitting a 1.0 no artifact supports -- the value standing in for a measurement that this row's :statement forbids in the same sentence that asks for the producers. THE REPLACEMENT, narrow: \"(:measured, 3/3, risk_mis 3.333378732232873 on 4abad68c's observation)\" becomes \":measured with 3 of 3 criteria measurable on 4abad68c's observation, each observable's value being what its artifact says, and every disagreement with U21's probe named per-observable together with the artifact that decides it\". Today that reads: 2 of 3 agree, :registry-gap-list-present 0.0 against the probe's 1.0, risk_mis 6.666712065566529. NOTHING ELSE IN THE ACCEPTANCE MOVES -- three producers at the assembly point, one test per producer against a real artifact, a typed absence rather than a default, the live-pin rule, gates green -- and all of those were already met at 9973bba, which is why this pass changes no code. NO REGISTRY EDIT AND NO RULING IS WRITTEN: the repair that would make 3.333378732232873 the honest number is a gap-list pointer in aif-equations.edn, that is a registry write and Joe's, and it stays exactly where the first pass left it. REPRODUCED, not asserted: clojure -M holes/labs/wm-contract/u42_gauge_producers.clj /tmp/U42-verify exits 0 and prints registry-gap-list-present 0.0 (basis no-registry-pointer), reporting-gate-test-result 0.0, worklist-acceptance-state 1.0, the 2/3 agreement table, and 4abad68c measured 3/3 at risk_mis 6.666712065566529. Both arms of the 0.0 judgement are already pinned by tests (mission_gauges_test.clj:102-143): the real registry returning 0.0 with :no-registry-pointer, a planted pointer at a real file returning 1.0, a pointer at nothing returning 0.0, and an unreadable registry returning an absence with no :value."
