   :statement "MINTED BY U21. Under FUTON_WM_SELECTION_FOCUS the tick's focus is its own decision while the durable clock edge still names the previous tick's mission, and NOTHING closes the gap: record-selection-clock! (war_machine.clj:1786) fires after the trace is written, fire-and-forget, and a failure resolves silently inside the future (the zaif S4 write-half noted this and deferred it). So :mission-focus and :active-mission disagree on 3 of 3 recorded ticks, U21 records the disagreement as :agrees-with-durable? false, and no reader acts on it. Two parts: (a) reconcile -- decide and implement what the tick does when the projection and the witnessed edge disagree, including when the async write never lands (the honest options are a same-tick witnessed edge, a typed pending state, or a recorded divergence that a later tick clears; U21 deliberately chose none of them); (b) render -- render-active-mission-line (war_machine.clj:3856) reports the durable clock only, so an operator reading the report cannot see which mission the tick actually focused on. NOT a clock-minting row by default: a clock edge is witnessed evidence, and any minting this row proposes needs its witness rule named."
