   :statement "WHAT DOES THE S4 RECORD DO TO policyPosteriorImportsPolicyF (H4)? U27's audit found exactly one hole whose declared observation is already on persisted record, and it cannot be dispositioned because the declaration's two fields point opposite ways. THE RECORD: runs/2026-09-01-s4/wm-trace-s4.edn carries :f-pi-posterior {:coverage :complete, :join-key :action-type-and-target, :candidate-count 145, :uncovered-count 0, :status :present, :scaling :unscaled, :applied? true} with per-candidate :f-pi-by-candidate-id on 3 of its 4 ticks; the 4th records {:status :absent, :reason :incomplete-coverage, :uncovered-count 1, :applied? false} rather than imputing a value, and RUN9's replay control reproduces each record's own posterior at delta 0.0 (C470-s4-live-f-pi.md). THE AMBIGUITY: the declaration's evidence field asks for \"a run record whose Q(pi) carries a per-policy F term alongside E and G\" and its falsifier field says \"a run record in which Q(pi) is computed with an F_pi term from the observations under each policy\" -- the SAME observation, so one field calls it the discharge and the other calls it the refutation (Holes.lean:6650-6651, and the same shape at :6647-6648 for H3). On twelve of the fifteen holes the falsifier field genuinely refutes -- dirichletAccumulationImportAbsent even says outright \"the claim held open is the ABSENCE\" -- so H3/H4 are the exception, not the convention. Both readings END in a close under this contract's precedent, since enactedActionEqualsSelected was closed by REFUTATION on 2026-09-01 (mkRefutedByRecord), but they close it as opposite things and a reader of Figure 3 would draw opposite conclusions. A THIRD CONSIDERATION NEITHER FIELD MENTIONS: FUTON_WM_FPI_POSTERIOR is default-off (war_machine.clj:220 refuses the flag without the dark chain), so the record shows what the machine does UNDER A FLAG, not what it does. H3's contrast is what makes the pair worth ruling together: its wiring exists too, but no persisted record carries it -- S3 is a replay, its one live tau = beta tick ran under a write-suppressing preflight (run8_s3_preflight.clj:28-54), and all 18 :tau-source values in data/wm-trace/wm-trace-2026-09-01.edn are :selection-gain-only. CARRIED HERE TOO, because it is the same declarations' text: four pointers inside the H3/H4 docstrings have drifted. policy.clj:242-245 and :242-246, cited by both as the policy score seam, now land on gap-report; the seam is selection-scores at policy.clj:157. war_machine.clj:4450-4451 (the Laplace F binding) is now :5543, and :4452 (the :R8 route tag) is now :5857, where it names futon2.aif.free-energy/compute-prediction-error rather than the compute-variational-free-energy the 2026-08-30 receipt recorded. selection_gain.clj:187-193 still holds exactly, so the family cannot be re-resolved by offset. And H4's sentence \"there is no F term in it, and no free-energy symbol anywhere in the scoring path\" is now false of the seam: policy.clj:158 writes the score as ln E(a) - G(a)/tau [- F_pi(a)] and :184 takes :f-pi-policy-posterior? and :f-pi-values as options, landed by RUN9/I2 after the docstring was written. U27 did not repair any of it, because editing a Joe-ruled declaration's content is exactly what U26's review verified had not happened."
