   :evidence "REVIEW REPAIR (2026-09-04), TAKEN FIRST BECAUSE IT IS WHAT THE ROW WAS REOPENED ON: futon2 2698dc02 (the accepted run names one conformance measurement) and 7c7ff158 (the deposit replay, and the account). THE FIX WAS RIGHT AND LANDED ONE PASS TOO LATE: 82276605 committed the RUN3-once repair to wm_step.sh:435-446 together with the artifacts of the very pass that had exposed the non-idempotence, so the run store named :checked-at 2026-09-04T16:40:59.705961817Z in conformance.edn and in u49/04-controls.edn while the append-only ledger's :run-conformance row (seq 17) cites 2026-09-04T16:40:36.011998629Z -- the measurement u49 transcribed when that row landed. THE LEDGER IS THE AUTHORITY AND THE ARTIFACTS MOVED TO IT, not the other way: seq 17 cannot be rewritten, so conformance.edn and u49/04-controls.edn were restored to 16:40:36 and runs/latest-conformance.edn moved with them (it held 16:31:58, a THIRD re-measurement of the same run). Nothing but the timestamp differs across the three: same :conformant, 1 record / 9 hops / 9 distinct / 22 drawn / 19 unfired, same control-map sha b1246f2 -- three readings of one unchanged run store. THE REPLAY NOW SHOWS THE PROPERTY THE ROW CLAIMED: wm_step.sh deposit re-runs the battery with RUN3 SKIPPED (runs/2026-09-04-010-accepted/battery.log:11), all EIGHT catalogued checks :already-present at their existing seqs -- run-conformance 17 (battery.log:22-24), tensions-cashed 18, selection-discrimination 19, contract-pin 20, flip-readiness 21, per-node-runtime-validation 22, enumeration-completeness 23, rationale-regret 24 -- every :row/sha unchanged, every command exit=0, run_era_ledger.bb --check green. Nothing appended and nothing refused. THE ONE THING THAT SAYS THIS IS NOT A HAND-EDIT THAT HAPPENS TO MATCH: after the replay the working tree is dirty in battery.log ALONE, so every check -- u49's transcription included -- rewrote its receipt byte-for-byte, which makes the restored 04-controls.edn what u49 DERIVES from