  :evidence "DONE-UNREVIEWED. futon2 9d70a8b4 (runner, checker, both records, FUNDAMENTALS.edn, report) + p4ng cdbbae2 (negative controls section 12, pointer_check roots) + this commit (the ledger). THE FALSIFIER FIRED. FUNDAMENTALS.edn's :fundamental/machine-policy-carrier named it -- \"a runtime decision in which two or more cascades for one selected mission are constructed and scored\" -- and :F1 slice 2 had already RUN it over the corpus without it firing (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F1-machine-q/02-policy-family-census.edn:55-58: 234 of 889 decisions carry an :apply-cascade candidate, :most-distinct-cascades-for-one-target-in-one-record 1, :records-with-two-or-more-cascades-for-one-target 0). The probe was not blind and the absence was measured, which is what makes this record a change of state rather than a first look. THE PRODUCER: holes/labs/wm-contract/f7_cascade_policy_decision.clj:101-160 reads ONE RECORDED DECISION BY :run/id, takes the mission the machine committed to, builds |psi> with the LIVE LANE'S OWN builder (futon2.report.cascade-lane/mission->psi, scripts/futon2/report/cascade_lane.clj:306 -- not a psi invented for the occasion), constructs with cascade-lane/cascade-policy-menu-for (scripts/futon2/report/cascade_lane.clj:102-144, which shells to futon3a/holes/labs/M-memes-arrows/cascade_serve.py once per coverage-saturation epsilon and admits only COMPLETE untruncated distinct policies at the pool ceiling) and scores with futon2.aif.cascade-prior/shadow-rank (src/futon2/aif/cascade_prior.clj:163-207). NEITHER OF THOSE TWO PIECES IS NEW -- what was missing was a producer joining them to a decision the machine actually made, and before this row cascade-policy-menu-for had no caller outside its own 2-arity delegation (scripts/futon2/report/cascade_lane.clj:112) and a with-redefs test. THE RECORD: holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F7-cascade-policy/f7-cascade-policy-decision.edn, recorded run c149f9de-669c-4817-9b0e-ed4aad77db79 (data/wm-trace/wm-trace-2026-09-04.edn, 2026-09-04T07:50:47.952039102Z), committed target M-expressions-of-interest (f7-cascade-policy-decision.edn:144-153). :candidate-count 2, :policy-choice? true (:161-162). THE TWO POLICIES DIFFER IN BOTH PATTERN MEMBERSHIP AND WIRING, which is the diversity M-wm-aif-policy-grain-compliance.md:109 asks for: 23 patterns with a 7-edge :descent and 2 :co_app edges at epsilon 0.10, against 1 pattern with an empty semilattice at 0.20 (:5-137). The incumbent 0.15 produced the SAME identity as 0.20 and collapsed into it -- the menu does not pad. Both carry a finite :cascade-score (-6.901 and 0.019) and both are ranked with normalized weights (:186-265). :governed-by :cascade-score, and that is a limit rather than a result: the cascade prior is at COLD START (:samples 0, :172-184), so ln E(pi) is uniform and the habit leg has nothing to say yet. THE CHECK IS NOT \"COUNT THE CANDIDATES\": holes/labs/wm-contract/f7_cascade_choice_check.bb refuses thirteen ways of carrying two entries without offering a choice of policy -- :error/single-cascade, /duplicate-policy-identity, /forged-policy-key, /mixed-mission, /truncated-candidate, /unscored-candidate, /unranked, /ranking-population, /unnormalized-weights, /claims-enactment, /basis-does-not-match-record, /basis-run-not-found, /not-a-cascade-policy-decision. The interesting failure here is a FALSE TWO, not an absence. THE NEGATIVE CONTROL IS NOT A PLANT: --single runs the same pipeline over the same recorded decision at the production incumbent epsilon 0.15 only and gets exactly one cascade (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F7-cascade-policy/f7-single-cascade-decision.edn:52 :candidate-count 1, :34 :menu-status :no-policy-choice, :77 :selection nil). That is the shape of all 889 recorded decisions. CONTROLS, negative_controls.sh section 12, 13 negative + 2 positive (suite 75/43 -> 88/45). THREE MUTATION-TESTED, AND TWO OF THE THREE SHOWED THE REFUSAL IS OVER-DETERMINED, reported rather than glossed: neutering the fewer-than-two refusal still refuses the one-cascade record, as :error/unranked, because shadow-rank refuses fewer than two policies by design (src/futon2/aif/cascade_prior.clj:176-179) so there is no ranking to record; neutering the basis comparison still refuses the planted target, as :error/mixed-mission. THE ONE WITH NO SECOND LINE IS 12g: neutering the policy-key recomputation ACCEPTS a hand-edited :policy-key. 12o IS THE TRANSCRIPTION CONTROL and it is what keeps the checker honest: f7_cascade_choice_check.bb carries a copy of cascade-prior/policy-key so it runs under bb without the futon2 classpath (the same trade f1_policy_family_census.bb makes for habit-prior/policy-key), and a drifted copy would still refuse and still accept -- on the wrong identities -- so the real namespace is loaded once and its keys compared with the record's. THE CENSUS ENTRY MOVED, :in -> :out with :criterion-leg-that-fails :lean (FUNDAMENTALS.edn:243-296; counts 11 entries, 7 :in / 4 :out -> 6 :in / 5 :out). The criterion is a CONJUNCTION -- uninhabited in BOTH Lean and the runtime -- and the runtime side is now inhabited by a producer, a scorer and an actual record, which is the standard :out/realized-outcome-channel closed its runtime leg by and not a schema. THE SENTENCE THAT WAS THE STRONGEST EVIDENCE FOR THE OLD VERDICT NOW READS THE OTHER WAY, and it is the same sentence: src/futon2/aif/cascade_prior.clj:1-12 says live use is valid only after the machine exposes two or more admissible cascades for one selected mission AND supplies an honest cascade-level score. It states a CONDITION; both clauses are met by the record; what follows is that live use would now be VALID, not that it has been taken. WHAT THE MOVE DOES NOT SAY, four limits in the entry's own :what-is-still-open (FUNDAMENTALS.edn:280-284): nothing selects or enacts a cascade (the record's :enacted? is false, the production lane still constructs one cascade per target, and the advisory lane that would carry cascades into a t